# Differential Practice (MeWorld game)

**Entry:** Welcome → Differentials · `Home.jsx` eager-imports `DifferentialPractice.jsx` (no lazy — CSS guard).

## Data sources (critical)

| What | Path | Used by |
|------|------|---------|
| **Clean LLM cases (canonical)** | `C:\Users\steve\MeWorld\data\cases\case_N.json` | Build only |
| **Differential review bank** | `game/src/data/differentialReview.json` | Case tab |
| **Practice cards** | `game/src/data/differentialBank.json` | Chief complaint + answer key |
| **Real-world stories** | `game/src/data/realWorldCases.json` | Real World tab |
| **Runtime play cases (thin)** | `game/data/cases/` + `preparedCases.json` | Play/Briefing only — **not** differential Case tab |

Rebuild review bank after clean JSON changes:
```powershell
Set-Location C:\Users\steve\MeWorld\game
node scripts/build-differential-review.mjs
```
Or `npm run build:differential-review` (included in `build:data` / `predev`).

**Do not** parse `*_ocr.txt` for differential Case tab — use `case_N.json` via build script.

## Study panel tabs

`DifferentialStudyPanel.jsx` — **text labels** (not icons): Review · Timeline · Case · Notes · Real World.

1. **Review** — bookmark queue jump list
2. **Timeline** — practice attempt history + voice notes
3. **Case** — `DifferentialReviewPanel`: Case Summary + **numbered Orders** (1, 2, 3… workflow)
4. **Notes** — shared case journal (same store as immersive play)
5. **Real World** — up to 2 curated patient stories + YouTube iframes + search fallback

## Preflight — enforced on every `npm run dev`

**Do not bypass.** `npm run dev` runs this chain automatically; servers **stop** if any step fails:

| Step | What |
|------|------|
| 1 | `build:data` + `smoke-test.mjs` (data + queue logic) |
| 2 | `smoke-pre-serve.mjs` (CSS audit + **`vite build`**) |
| 3 | Free ports → start API → **`smoke:differential`** |
| 4 | Start Vite → **`smoke:differential-session`** (screenshots) |
| 5 | Only then: keep serving at http://localhost:5173/ |

Pass criteria:
- **`vite build`** exits 0 (JS syntax/duplicate `const` → blank white app)
- CSS audit clean
- `GET /api/voice-note/status` → **`batch: true`**, **`merge: true`**
- Session smoke: `.diff-practice` **rgb(12, 12, 16)**, record button visible
- Screenshots: `docs/smoke-screenshots/<date>/`

**URLs:** http://localhost:5173/ only — if Vite would bind elsewhere, port free failed; fix before serving.

If voice-note fails: fix `game/server/voiceNoteTranscribe.js` — dev will not stay up until green.

## Patient names

- Templates use `{{patient_name}}` in clean JSON HPI.
- Runtime: `personalizeDifferentialReview()` in `src/lib/differentialReview.js`
- Name region from **Settings → audience profile** (`readAudienceProfile().nameRegion`)
- **Default region:** `mixed` (NYC / multicultural — one culture per case #)
- Also applies refined HPI from `narrativeRefine.js` when user has agreed refined narrative saved.

## UI conventions

- Chief complaint: **2 lines** — complaint + specialty/setting (`splitChiefComplaintHeadline`)
- ICU ambience: `unlockAmbience` + `startIcuMonitor` on enter; volume control **fixed bottom-right**, no border box (`.diff-ambience-dock`)
- Orders: structured list with gold step numbers — not `[OK]` text blocks
- CSS: `src/styles/differential-practice.css` — audit via `scripts/audit-component-css.mjs`

## Real World tab — tiered stories + video repair

On tab open: `POST /api/differential/real-world` → `server/realWorldProvider.js`

**Default stack (no Gemini billing):**

| Layer | Provider | Env |
|-------|----------|-----|
| **Stories** | **DeepSeek** | `REAL_WORLD_PROVIDER=deepseek` + `DEEPSEEK_API_KEY` |
| **YouTube videos** | **YouTube Data API** (if `YOUTUBE_API_KEY`) or **yt-search** | `REAL_WORLD_VIDEO_PROVIDER=youtube-api` (auto when key set) |

Do **not** use Gemini for Real World unless Steve explicitly opts in — free tier is 20 req/day.

| Provider | When | Strength |
|----------|------|----------|
| **DeepSeek** (default) | `deepseekRealWorld.js` | Good story text; videos via yt-search |
| **Gemini** (optional) | `REAL_WORLD_PROVIDER=gemini` + `REAL_WORLD_VIDEO_PROVIDER=auto` | Google Search grounding — quota limited |

Env (`MeWorld/.env`):
- `DEEPSEEK_API_KEY` — stories (required for Real World tab)
- `REAL_WORLD_PROVIDER=deepseek`
- `REAL_WORLD_VIDEO_PROVIDER=yt-search` — **default**; never hits Gemini quota
- `GEMINI_API_KEY` — optional; ignored for video when `yt-search` is set
- `REAL_WORLD_VIDEO_PROVIDER=auto` — only if Steve wants Gemini video repair (paid/quota)

**Two tiers per case (always aim for both):**
1. **`direct`** — real patient matching CCS diagnosis (e.g. Alex Lewis / TSS)
2. **`adjacent`** — broader real public story teaching around the topic (e.g. water-safety advocacy for drowning Case 113). **Never default to Michael Phelps** on unrelated cases — DeepSeek anchor-biased on that example; use `realWorldStoryQuality.js` + `purge-phelps-real-world-cache.mjs`.

Video plug-in: `youtubeSearchRepair.js` — **yt-search** by default (free). Optional Gemini when `REAL_WORLD_VIDEO_PROVIDER=auto|gemini`. Scoring is stricter for `direct`, looser for `adjacent`. Cache: `game/.real-world-cache/case_N.json` — use Refresh in UI or `refresh: true` after rule changes.

**Curated:** `src/data/realWorldCases.json` — hand-verified `tier` + `match.caseIds`. UI merges curated + API via `mergeStoriesByTier`.

